d.paragraphs[2].text='Research hypothesis • Revised 9 September 2026 • Interaction and stability extensions'
d.paragraphs[4].text=('We investigate a physically nonexpanding universe with conditional temporal redshift 1+z=exp(κr). Multiplicative composition fixes this form but neither determines κ nor establishes a microscopic interaction. The preserved 164-group experiment uses 104 training, 35 validation and 25 final-test objects. Its fitted κ=7.7314966×10⁻⁵ per million light-years gives final-test redshift RMSE 412.441 km/s versus 411.934 km/s for the specified expanding reference, an unresolved difference. The explicit matter–light interaction fails intended exact atomic invariance: preserving leading optical binding changes hyperfine response. A compensating magnetic moment repairs only the leading term. Shared photon/tensor propagation remains a replacement requirement; universal conformal coupling protects local matter physics but cancels homogeneous redshift when material geometry is static. The fixed flat brightness law develops a significant correlated residual trend in 960 higher-redshift supernovae. Fitting negative curvature improves χ² from 898.5 to 873.0, while positive curvature prefers the flat limit; no compatible stable nonexpanding solution has been demonstrated. In Einstein gravity, the preferred static negative curvature requires negative total enthalpy, which a minimally coupled P(φ,X) scalar cannot supply with both healthy kinetic and gradient terms in the tested regime. Five candidate mechanisms remain documented. Processed duration data favor whole-signal stretching, while FIRAS constrains the tested thermal mixtures; neither identifies the field. New toy extensions show that higher spatial gradients plus a restoring term can stabilize one mode, and that thermal relaxation can approach the monopole spectrum but erases distant source contrast if equally strong at optical frequencies. These conditional results do not establish full gravitational stability, atomic protection or a CMB origin. Screening is a historical branch, not an ingredient of the present unscreened candidate. The next milestone remains one explicit nonrotating interaction with protected clock ratios, shared propagation and a stable background, deriving brightness and angular distances together.')
